      "content": "Interesting. So you're saying that the model shouldn't just look at economic data (like tax history), but should also proactively factor in how the community's existing social perceptions and biases regarding race might affect a person's \"stability\" or \"value.\"\n\nTo clarify, you're suggesting that the algorithm should essentially bake in these social realities—like the \"suspicion or mistrust\" you mentioned—as part of the mathematical weighting? How would a developer actually quantify that \"community perception\" variable in the code to ensure the model is being \"realistic\" about social stability?",
